structor.\"},\"input_at_zero\":{\"type\":[\"number\",\"null\"],\"description\":\"Optional explicit input value at zero output. A number here, unlike the incremental and average-rate variants, where it is a time series reference.\"}},\"required\":[\"function_data\",\"curve_type\"],\"title\":\"TimeSeriesInputOutputCurve\",\"description\":\"A time-series-backed input-output curve. The static counterpart is InputOutputCurve.\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"TimeSeriesLinearFunctionData\":{\"description\":\"Time-series-backed variant of `LinearFunctionData`. In place of inline coefficients it carries `association_id`, referencing a stored series that supplies them at each step; use it when the coefficients change over time.\",\"properties\":{\"function_type\":{\"const\":\"TIME_SERIES_LINEAR\",\"type\":\"string\",\"default\":\"TIME_SERIES_LINEAR\"},\"association_id\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"description\":\"Store-minted id of the time series association whose values supply this function data over time. Resolved against the accompanying time series store on read; minted by that store and meaningful only against it, never assigned by a document producer.\"}},\"required\":[\"function_type\",\"association_id\"],\"title\":\"TimeSeriesLinearFunctionData\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"TimeSeriesPiecewiseLinearData\":{\"description\":\"Time-series-backed variant of `PiecewiseLinearData`. In place of an inline point table it carries `association_id`, referencing a stored series that supplies one at each step; use it when the points change over time.\",\"properties\":{\"function_type\":{\"const\":\"TIME_SERIES_PIECEWISE_LINEAR\",\"type\":\"string\",\"default\":\"TIME_SERIES_PIECEWISE_LINEAR\"},\"association_id\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"description\":\"Store-minted id of the time series association whose values supply this function data over time. Resolved against the accompanying time series store on read; minted by that store and meaningful only against it, never assigned by a document producer.\"}},\"required\":[\"function_type\",\"association_id\"],\"title\":\"TimeSeriesPiecewiseLinearData\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"TimeSeriesPiecewiseStepData\":{\"description\":\"Time-series-backed variant of `PiecewiseStepData`. In place of inline coordinate vectors it carries `association_id`, referencing a stored series that supplies them at each step; use it when the segments change over time.\",\"properties\":{\"function_type\":{\"const\":\"TIME_SERIES_PIECEWISE_STEP\",\"type\":\"string\",\"default\":\"TIME_SERIES_PIECEWISE_STEP\"},\"association_id\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"description\":\"Store-minted id of the time series association whose values supply this function data over time. Resolved against the accompanying time series store on read; minted by that store and meaningful only against it, never assigned by a document producer.\"}},\"required\":[\"function_type\",\"association_id\"],\"title\":\"TimeSeriesPiecewiseStepData\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"TimeSeriesQuadraticFunctionData\":{\"description\":\"Time-series-backed variant of `QuadraticFunctionData`. In place of inline coefficients it carries `association_id`, referencing a stored series that supplies them at each step; use it when the coefficients change over time.\",\"properties\":{\"function_type\":{\"const\":\"TIME_SERIES_QUADRATIC\",\"type\":\"string\",\"default\":\"TIME_SERIES_QUADRATIC\"},\"association_id\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"description\":\"Store-minted id of the time series association whose values supply this function data over time. Resolved against the accompanying time series store on read; minted by that store and meaningful only against it, never assigned by a document producer.\"}},\"required\":[\"function_type\",\"association_id\"],\"title\":\"TimeSeriesQuadraticFunctionData\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"TurbinePump\":{\"description\":\"A pair of values, one for the turbine (generating) mode and one for the pump (charging) mode of a pumped hydro unit.\",\"properties\":{\"turbine\":{\"type\":\"number\"},\"pump\":{\"type\":\"number\"}},\"required\":[\"turbine\",\"pump\"],\"title\":\"TurbinePump\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"UnitSystem\":{\"description\":\"Unit basis a stored value is expressed in. COMPONENT_BASE: per-unit against a base the component records itself. NATURAL_UNITS: the quantity's own physical unit. No system-wide option: a value per-unitized against a shared base records that base on the component and rides as COMPONENT_BASE. Used in three scopes, each read against its own record rather than a document-wide table: a component's own `power_units` (against that component's `base_power`), a cost payload's own `power_units` (e.g. `CostCurve`, against the owning component's `base_power`), and a time series association's own `unit_system` (governing only that one series).\",\"enum\":[\"COMPONENT_BASE\",\"NATURAL_UNITS\"],\"title\":\"UnitSystem\",\"type\":\"string\"},\"UpDown\":{\"description\":\"A pair of values, one for the upward (`up`) and one for the downward (`down`) direction of a quantity.\",\"properties\":{\"down\":{\"title\":\"Down\",\"type\":\"number\"},\"up\":{\"title\":\"Up\",\"type\":\"number\"}},\"required\":[\"up\",\"down\"],\"title\":\"UpDown\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"ValueCurve\":{\"description\":\"A cost or fuel curve: function data plus a declaration of how to read its y axis. `INPUT_OUTPUT` reads y as the total `f(x)`, `INCREMENTAL` as the marginal rate `f'(x)`, and `AVERAGE_RATE` as the average `f(x)/x`; the three can express the same underlying function and are inter-convertible given `initial_input`. The `TIME_SERIES_*` variants are the time-varying equivalents. Which form to use follows the data source: bid stacks are incremental, total cost tables input-output, efficiency tables average rate.\",\"discriminator\":{\"mapping\":{\"AVERAGE_RATE\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/external-1e9a0d19d7563e537121.json#/\$defs/AverageRateCurve\",\"INCREMENTAL\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/external-1e9a0d19d7563e537121.json#/\$defs